  "findings": [
    "C1 prepare_tests.js pairs latin1 input and latin1 output; this is a byte-preserving adapter for mixed legacy encodings, not a UTF-8 decoder. ASCII transformations preserve unrelated bytes.",
    "verify_scope.js pairs latin1 Git stdout and latin1 complete.diff output. SHA-256 operates on raw bytes.",
    "prepare_map.js uses latin1 only for normalized comparison; source copies remain raw Buffer writes.",
    "Study prepare_study.js copies raw Buffers, except ASCII SMS.qsf SEED substitution; no RTL decode/re-encode.",
    "prepare_phases.js and prepare_nonfm.js handle generated UTF-8 fixtures, not the five production RTL files.",
    "Historical port.js also pairs latin1 read/write; reviewed read-only. No defective latin1-to-default-UTF8 source-write path was found in these relevant scripts. No evidence identifies which earlier operation corrupted the out-of-scope main-workspace file."
